# Q4: Action A: Turn the head towards the "threat" (i.e., looking past the blocking arm). This adds intent and context, suggesting the robot is aware of what it's blocking. Action B: Lower the torso slightly. This could make the robot look more grounded and braced for impact. Winner is Action A because it adds a stronger narrative element and makes the protective gesture more intelligent and directed.
